# Rust Development

## Installation

```bash
# Default: rustup from official CDN
curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh -s -- -y

# China mirror (USTC) — use when default CDN is slow or blocked:
export RUSTUP_DIST_SERVER=https://mirrors.ustc.edu.cn/rust-static
export RUSTUP_UPDATE_ROOT=https://mirrors.ustc.edu.cn/rust-static/rustup
curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh -s -- -y

# Alternative mirrors:
#   Tsinghua: https://mirrors.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn/rustup
#   Shanghai Jiao Tong: https://mirrors.sjtug.sjtu.edu.cn/rust-static
#   Aliyun: https://mirrors.aliyun.com/rustup

# Verify
source "$HOME/.cargo/env"
rustc --version && cargo --version

# Update
rustup update

# Nightly (for unstable features)
rustup toolchain install nightly
rustup default nightly  # or: cargo +nightly build
```

### Cargo Basics

```bash
cargo new my-project           # binary
cargo new my-lib --lib         # library
cargo build                    # debug
cargo build --release          # optimized
cargo run                      # build + run
cargo test                     # run tests
cargo bench                    # benchmarks
cargo doc --open               # generate docs
cargo check                    # type-check only (fast)
cargo clippy                   # lint
cargo fmt                      # format
cargo add <crate>              # add dependency
cargo add <crate> --features <feat>
cargo tree                     # dependency tree
cargo update                   # update Cargo.lock
```

## Core Language Concepts

### Ownership & Borrowing

```rust
// Ownership: one owner at a time
let s1 = String::from("hello");
let s2 = s1;           // s1 moved, s1 is invalid
// println!("{s1}");   // compile error!

// Borrowing: temporary access
let s = String::from("hello");
let r1 = &s;            // immutable borrow
let r2 = &s;            // multiple immutable borrows OK
// let r3 = &mut s;     // ERROR: can't mutable borrow while immutable borrows exist

// Lifetimes: compiler tracks how long references live
fn longest<'a>(x: &'a str, y: &'a str) -> &'a str {
    if x.len() > y.len() { x } else { y }
}
```

### Traits & Generics

```rust
// Trait: shared behavior interface
trait Summary {
    fn summarize(&self) -> String;
    fn default_summary(&self) -> String {  // default impl
        String::from("(Read more...)")
    }
}

impl Summary for NewsArticle {
    fn summarize(&self) -> String {
        format!("{}: {}", self.headline, self.author)
    }
}

// Trait bounds
fn notify<T: Summary>(item: &T) { }
fn notify2(item: &impl Summary) { }            // syntactic sugar
fn notify3<T>(item: &T) where T: Summary { }   // where clause

// Common traits
// Clone, Copy, Debug, Display, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord, Hash
// Default, From, Into, AsRef, AsMut, Deref, Drop, Send, Sync, Sized

// Send: type can be transferred across thread boundaries
// Sync: type can be shared between threads via reference (&T)
// Unpin: type can be moved after being pinned
```

### Smart Pointers

```rust
Box<T>       // heap allocation, fixed size, owns data
Rc<T>        // reference-counted, single-threaded shared ownership
Arc<T>       // atomic reference-counted, thread-safe shared ownership
RefCell<T>   // interior mutability, runtime borrow checking
Mutex<T>     // mutual exclusion, thread-safe
RwLock<T>    // read-write lock, multiple readers
Cow<'a, T>   // clone-on-write — borrow or own as needed
Pin<T>       // prevent move (needed for async)

// Common pattern: Arc<Mutex<T>> for shared mutable state across threads
let shared = Arc::new(Mutex::new(0));
let clone = shared.clone();
tokio::spawn(async move {
    let mut val = clone.lock().await;
    *val += 1;
});
```

## Async Runtime

### Tokio (dominant async runtime)

```toml
[dependencies]
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }
```

```rust
#[tokio::main]
async fn main() {
    // Spawn concurrent tasks
    let handle = tokio::spawn(async {
        "hello from task"
    });
    let result = handle.await.unwrap();

    // Join multiple futures
    let (r1, r2) = tokio::join!(
        async { compute_a().await },
        async { compute_b().await },
    );

    // Select first completed
    tokio::select! {
        result = long_task() => { /* handle result */ }
        _ = tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_secs(5)) => {
            println!("timeout!");
        }
    }

    // Channels
    let (tx, mut rx) = tokio::sync::mpsc::channel(32);  // bounded
    tx.send("msg").await.unwrap();
    let msg = rx.recv().await.unwrap();

    // broadcast, watch, oneshot channels also available
    // tokio::sync::broadcast — fan-out
    // tokio::sync::watch    — single-producer, latest value
    // tokio::sync::oneshot  — single value, one receiver
}

async fn compute_a() -> String { todo!() }
async fn compute_b() -> String { todo!() }
async fn long_task() -> String { todo!() }
```

### Streams (async iterators)

```rust
use tokio_stream::StreamExt;
use futures::stream;

let stream = stream::iter(vec![1, 2, 3]);
tokio::pin!(stream);

while let Some(val) = stream.next().await {
    println!("{val}");
}

// Common stream operations
stream.map(|x| x * 2)
stream.filter(|x| async { x % 2 == 0 })
stream.buffer_unordered(10)  // concurrent processing
stream.chunks_timeout(100, Duration::from_millis(50))
```

### Other Async Runtimes

```rust
// async-std — simpler, std-like API
use async_std::task;
task::spawn(async { });

// smol — minimal, composable
use smol::Executor;
```

## Web Frameworks

### Axum (recommended — tokio-native, tower middleware)

```toml
[dependencies]
axum = "0.7"
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }
tower = "0.4"
serde = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }
```

```rust
use axum::{
    routing::{get, post},
    Router, Json, extract::{Path, Query, State},
    http::StatusCode,
};
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};

#[derive(Clone)]
struct AppState {
    db: sqlx::PgPool,
}

// Handler with state
async fn get_user(
    State(state): State<AppState>,
    Path(user_id): Path<i32>,
) -> Result<Json<User>, StatusCode> {
    let user = sqlx::query_as!(User, "SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1", user_id)
        .fetch_optional(&state.db)
        .await
        .map_err(|_| StatusCode::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR)?
        .ok_or(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND)?;
    Ok(Json(user))
}

// Middleware
use tower_http::cors::CorsLayer;
use tower_http::trace::TraceLayer;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() {
    let app = Router::new()
        .route("/", get(root))
        .route("/users/:id", get(get_user))
        .route("/users", post(create_user))
        .layer(TraceLayer::new_for_http())
        .layer(CorsLayer::permissive())
        .with_state(app_state);

    let listener = tokio::net::TcpListener::bind("0.0.0.0:3000").await.unwrap();
    axum::serve(listener, app).await.unwrap();
}
```

### Actix-web (high-performance actor model)

```toml
actix-web = "4"
actix-rt = "2"
serde = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }
```

```rust
use actix_web::{web, App, HttpServer, HttpResponse, middleware};

async fn index() -> HttpResponse {
    HttpResponse::Ok().body("Hello")
}

#[actix_web::main]
async fn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {
    HttpServer::new(|| {
        App::new()
            .wrap(middleware::Logger::default())
            .route("/", web::get().to(index))
    })
    .bind("127.0.0.1:8080")?
    .run()
    .await
}
```

### Other Web Frameworks

| Framework | Concurrency | Key Feature |
|---|---|---|
| **axum** | tokio + tower | Middleware ecosystem, type-safe |
| **actix-web** | Actor model | Battle-tested, high perf |
| **warp** | tokio | Filter combinator API |
| **rocket** | tokio | Macro-heavy, ergonomic |
| **poem** | tokio | OpenAPI-first, similar to axum |
| **salvo** | tokio | Chinese ecosystem, axum-inspired |

## Networking & RPC

### gRPC with Tonic

```toml
[dependencies]
tonic = "0.11"
prost = "0.12"
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }

[build-dependencies]
tonic-build = "0.11"
```

```rust
// Proto definition (proto/hello.proto):
// service Greeter { rpc SayHello(HelloRequest) returns (HelloReply); }

use tonic::{transport::Server, Request, Response, Status};
use hello::greeter_server::{Greeter, GreeterServer};

#[derive(Default)]
struct MyGreeter;

#[tonic::async_trait]
impl Greeter for MyGreeter {
    async fn say_hello(&self, req: Request<HelloRequest>)
        -> Result<Response<HelloReply>, Status> {
        let reply = HelloReply {
            message: format!("Hello {}!", req.into_inner().name),
        };
        Ok(Response::new(reply))
    }
}

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let addr = "[::1]:50051".parse()?;
    let greeter = MyGreeter::default();
    Server::builder()
        .add_service(GreeterServer::new(greeter))
        .serve(addr)
        .await?;
    Ok(())
}

// Bidi streaming (like ANDL ExpertCompute)
use tonic::Streaming;
async fn chat(&self, req: Request<Streaming<ChatMsg>>)
    -> Result<Response<Streaming<ChatMsg>>, Status> {
    let mut stream = req.into_inner();
    let (tx, rx) = tokio::sync::mpsc::channel(4);
    tokio::spawn(async move {
        while let Some(msg) = stream.message().await.unwrap() {
            tx.send(msg).await.unwrap();
        }
    });
    Ok(Response::new(tokio_stream::wrappers::ReceiverStream::new(rx)))
}
```

### QUIC with Quinn

```toml
quinn = "0.11"
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }
rustls = "0.23"
```

```rust
use quinn::{Endpoint, Connection};

// Server
let (endpoint, _incoming) = {
    let cert = rcgen::generate_simple_self_signed(vec!["localhost".into()])?;
    let server_crypto = rustls::ServerConfig::builder()
        .with_no_client_auth()
        .with_single_cert(vec![cert.cert.der().clone()], cert.key_pair.serialize_der()?.into())?;
    Endpoint::server(server_crypto, "[::1]:5000".parse()?)?
};

// Client
let mut endpoint = Endpoint::client("[::1]:0".parse()?)?;
let client_crypto = rustls::ClientConfig::builder()
    .dangerous()  // skip verification for local dev
    .with_custom_certificate_verifier(SkipServerVerification::new())
    .with_no_client_auth();
endpoint.set_default_client_config(client_crypto);

let conn = endpoint.connect(server_addr, "localhost")?.await?;
let (mut send, mut recv) = conn.open_bi().await?;
send.write_all(b"hello").await?;
send.finish().await?;
let reply = recv.read_to_end(1024).await?;
```

### TCP/TLS

```rust
// Raw TCP with tokio
let listener = tokio::net::TcpListener::bind("0.0.0.0:8080").await?;
loop {
    let (stream, addr) = listener.accept().await?;
    tokio::spawn(handle_connection(stream));
}

// TLS with tokio-rustls
use tokio_rustls::TlsAcceptor;
let acceptor = TlsAcceptor::from(tls_config);
let stream = acceptor.accept(stream).await?;

// DNS
use trust_dns_resolver::TokioAsyncResolver;
let resolver = TokioAsyncResolver::tokio_from_system_conf()?;
let ips = resolver.lookup_ip("example.com").await?;
```

## CLI Development

```toml
clap = { version = "4", features = ["derive"] }
```

```rust
use clap::{Parser, Subcommand};

#[derive(Parser)]
#[command(name = "andl-cli")]
#[command(about = "ANDL distributed inference CLI")]
struct Cli {
    #[command(subcommand)]
    command: Commands,

    #[arg(short, long, default_value = "info")]
    log_level: String,

    #[arg(short, long, default_value = "127.0.0.1")]
    host: String,
}

#[derive(Subcommand)]
enum Commands {
    /// Start the expert node
    Expert {
        #[arg(short, long)]
        shard_id: u32,
        #[arg(short, long)]
        model_path: PathBuf,
    },
    /// Start the global node
    Global {
        #[arg(short, long)]
        model_path: PathBuf,
    },
}

fn main() {
    let cli = Cli::parse();
    match &cli.command {
        Commands::Expert { shard_id, model_path } => {
            println!("Starting expert shard {shard_id}: {model_path:?}");
        }
        Commands::Global { model_path } => {
            println!("Starting global node: {model_path:?}");
        }
    }
}
```

## Error Handling

### thiserror (derive Error for custom types)

```rust
use thiserror::Error;

#[derive(Error, Debug)]
pub enum AndlError {
    #[error("connection failed: {0}")]
    Connection(String),

    #[error("expert {expert_id} not found in shard {shard_id}")]
    ExpertNotFound { expert_id: u32, shard_id: u32 },

    #[error("gRPC error")]
    Grpc(#[from] tonic::Status),

    #[error("I/O error")]
    Io(#[from] std::io::Error),

    #[error("unknown error")]
    Unknown,
}
```

### anyhow (flexible error handling for applications)

```rust
use anyhow::{Result, Context, bail, anyhow};

fn load_config(path: &str) -> Result<Config> {
    let content = std::fs::read_to_string(path)
        .with_context(|| format!("failed to read config from {path}"))?;
    let config: Config = toml::from_str(&content)?;
    if config.nodes.is_empty() {
        bail!("config must have at least one node");
    }
    Ok(config)
}
```

## Serialization

### Serde (dominant serialization framework)

```rust
use serde::{Serialize, Deserialize};

#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]
struct ExpertConfig {
    model_id: String,
    #[serde(rename = "n_experts")]
    num_experts: u32,
    shard_size: u32,
    #[serde(default)]
    hot_experts: Vec<u32>,
}

// Formats
let json = serde_json::to_string_pretty(&config)?;
let config: ExpertConfig = serde_json::from_str(&json)?;

let toml_str = toml::to_string(&config)?;
let yaml_str = serde_yaml::to_string(&config)?;

// Binary formats for performance
let bytes = bincode::serialize(&config)?;             // compact
let bytes = rmp_serde::to_vec(&config)?;               // MessagePack
let bytes = prost::Message::encode_to_vec(&proto_msg); // Protobuf
```

## Database

### SQLx (async, compile-time checked)

```toml
sqlx = { version = "0.7", features = ["runtime-tokio-rustls", "postgres"] }
```

```rust
use sqlx::PgPool;

let pool = PgPool::connect("postgres://user:pass@localhost/db").await?;

// Compile-time checked query
let user = sqlx::query_as!(User, "SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE id = $1", 1)
    .fetch_one(&pool).await?;

// Dynamic query
let users = sqlx::query_as::<_, User>("SELECT * FROM users WHERE age > $1")
    .bind(18)
    .fetch_all(&pool).await?;

// Transaction
let mut tx = pool.begin().await?;
sqlx::query!("INSERT INTO users (name) VALUES ($1)", "alice")
    .execute(&mut *tx).await?;
tx.commit().await?;
```

